    "title": "When is Easter 2026? Holiday is near",
    "text": "March 28, 2026, 5:00 a.m. MTNow that we are solidly into spring, Easter is near.The season can put giant chocolate bunnies, the eternal debates over Peeps and Cadbury eggs, and finding the right kind of jelly beans at the front of some people’s minds. Others focus on a fundamental event at the center of Christianity: the resurrection of Jesus Christ after his crucifixion.But calculating the exact date of Easter is complicated, using a centuries-old formula and different definitions of the lunar cycle and the start of spring than are commonly used. There are even two different calculations of the date of Easter depending on what form of Christianity someone observes.Here are key observances in the Easter season, along with background on how Easter’s date is calculated:When is Easter 2026?In 2026, Easter falls on April 5 for western Christian churches. This is the date most people in the U.S. mean when referring to Easter.Eastern Orthodox churches use the Julian calendar to calculate the date for Easter, and it typically falls later than western Easter. In 2026, Orthodox easter is April 12.Why does Easter’s date change every year?At its simplest, Easter for western churches falls on the first Sunday after the first full moon of spring. But there are several details about how that is calculated that can throw the date off from what you might get by trying to figure it out yourself.First, western churches always refer to March 21 as the spring equinox, even though the precise date can range from March 19 to 21.The first full moon on or after the equinox is called the Paschal Moon. Because lunar cycles are 29.5 days, the astronomical full moon could fall anywhere from March 21 to April 19. However, churches also use ecclesiastical lunar tables that vary slightly from the astronomical ones, meaning the full moon’s date used for calculating Easter can be a day off from the Gregorian calendar. In the end, Easter could fall between March 22 and April 25, depending on the date of the full moon.Orthodox churches use a similar formula but use the Julian calendar as a reference for the first day of spring. March 21 on the Julian calendar translates to April 3 on the Gregorian calendar.What are future Easter dates?Here are the next few for western and Orthodox churches:2027: March 28 (May 2 Orthodox)2028: April 16 (April 16 Orthodox)2029: April 1 (April 8 Orthodox)What other Christian religious observances are tied to Easter’s date?Several Christian observances occur in the run-up to Easter. They include:Lent is the 40-day period of fasting, prayer and reflection that ends on Easter. Many Christians choose to give up something or commit to perform acts of service during this period.The first day of Lent is Ash Wednesday, when many Christians receive ashes on their foreheads as sign of penance.Palm Sunday is the Sunday before Easter and the start of Holy Week.Good Friday, which commemorates the death of Jesus, falls two days before Easter.Nate Trela covers trending news in Colorado and Utah for the USA TODAY Network.",
